WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.125
Step three collects Azure from the day-one
fixtures, as of November ninth, 2026.

2
00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:10.959
Five notices, all open, two needing
action: one each of advisory,

3
00:00:10.959 --> 00:00:14.750
incident, maintenance,
retirement and security.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:19.947
Five notices from six rows, because the
incident appears in two subscriptions,

5
00:00:19.947 --> 00:00:22.425
and the kit merges rows by tracking I D.

6
00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:26.188
Without that merge, the same
outage would become two tasks.

7
00:00:26.188 --> 00:00:28.188
Step four reads the records.

8
00:00:28.188 --> 00:00:32.688
The incident is a virtual machine
connectivity issue in East U S.

9
00:00:32.688 --> 00:00:38.538
The advisory asks clients of Azure
Storage to move to T L S 1.2 or later.

10
00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:42.676
The maintenance is planned work on
virtual machines in East U S 2.

11
00:00:42.676 --> 00:00:46.681
The retirement, of Basic S
K U public I P addresses,

12
00:00:46.681 --> 00:00:51.288
is due on September thirtieth,
2027, at the advisory's end.

13
00:00:51.288 --> 00:00:56.305
And the security advisory, for
Azure Kubernetes Service clusters,

14
00:00:56.305 --> 00:00:59.930
needs action with no date,
for the ISSO to review.
